@flexiarg problems/process-conduct-is-unassured
@title Problem node: the WM's process conduct is unassured
@keywords problem-node, process, handoff, assurance, traps
@audience futon stack operators, library authors
@tone plain
@style pattern
@why record authority: futon2 holes problems P-assured-process.md, S1 problem record (drafted by claude-1 from Joe's direction 2026-09-05; S1 fields are Joe's to confirm or rewrite; no library pattern grounds this node)
@how no mechanism claimed at problem grain; what solving requires is the record's solved-field (Lean process spec checked at every transition, typed handoff contracts, author-never-closes-own-handoff, stepper boundary, T5 reflexivity)

! conclusion: This is a problem-stating node: the WM's assurance stack covers the control loop's decisions and nothing assures its process conduct — the commissioning, returning, closing, and surfacing of delegated work.

  + context: Minted by library-loop row L5 from P-assured-process.md; it exists so @why edges from process-handling patterns have a problem node to land on.

  + IF:
    The WM, in operation, commissions work, receives returns, closes records, and surfaces results.

  + HOWEVER:
    The problem, per the record: the WM in operation is an orchestrator whose assurance stack (run-era ledger, catalogued checks, conformance certificates, stepper) covers the CONTROL LOOP's decisions; nothing yet assures its PROCESS conduct — and the eight-trap catalogue (N-process-trap-recording-conventions section 1) was harvested from precisely this class of activity, performed by this campaign's own agents with far more context than the machine will have. Handoff machinery exists un-assured (bells, parks, packets are prose conventions, not typed objects any checker refuses on); the tick's closure boundary excludes the seven store-owning namespaces of the full-loop click path; and T7/T8 have no WM instances today and no checker that would refuse one. (source: futon2 holes problems P-assured-process.md, S1, Joe's commissioning question of 2026-09-05 quoted in section 0)

  + THEN:
    Treat this node as the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer process-conduct assurance; solving the problem is scoped by the record's solved-field, not by this node.

  + BECAUSE:
    The record's own caveat applies to this node too: until a checker refuses process work that lacks these assurances, this node is prose — but prose with a committed source pointer.
    + evidence: futon2 holes problems P-assured-process.md, section 0 (Joe, verbatim, 2026-09-05) and section 1 S1 problem/now fields.
